<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Areopolis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tsimova</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Areopolis, formerly Tsimova, is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> peninsula of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, and was the seat of the Mavromichalis family. On 17 March 1821 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrobey-mavromichalis">Petrobey Mavromichalis</a> raised the flag of revolt there, one of the first acts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a>; the town was later renamed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ares">Ares</a>, the god of war. Its stone tower houses are typical of the Mani.</p></div>
